 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nSchema Column Visibility Issue\n\nDescription\n\nHello team,\n\nI've encountered an issue with the column visibility feature in the schema module. It seems that the recent changes have affected how columns are retrieved when the `only_visible` flag is set to `True`. Specifically, the columns that should be visible are not being filtered correctly, leading to unexpected results.\n\nHere's a minimal example to reproduce the issue:\n\n```python\nfrom sqlglot import Schema\n\n# Assuming `schema` is an instance of the Schema class\ntable_name = \"example_table\"\ncolumns = schema.get_columns(table_name, only_visible=True)\n\nprint(columns)  # Expected: ['visible_column1', 'visible_column2'], but got: ['visible_column1', 'visible_column2', 'invisible_column']\n```\n\nIn this example, even though `only_visible` is set to `True`, the output includes columns that should be invisible. This behavior is inconsistent with the expected functionality where only visible columns should be returned.\n\nIt would be great if someone could take a look at this. Let me know if you need more information or if there's anything else I can do to help debug this issue. Thanks!\n</issue>\n",
